          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 6"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.122,
            0.496,
            0.15
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "3.4 Playing with Digits"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.164,
            0.884,
            0.208
          ],
          "content": "We start writing numbers from 1, 2, 3 … and so on. There are nine 1-digit numbers."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.214,
            0.884,
            0.26
          ],
          "content": "Find out how many numbers have two digits, three digits, four digits, and five digits."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.169,
            0.263,
            0.879,
            0.392
          ],
          "content": "| 1-digitnumbers From 1-9 | 2-digitnumbers | 3-digitnumbers | 4-digitnumbers | 5-digitnumbers |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 9 |  |  |  |  |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_table_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.416,
            0.445,
            0.437
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Digit sums of numbers"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.445,
            0.59,
            0.512
          ],
          "content": "Komal observes that when she adds up digits of certain numbers the sum is the same."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.513,
            0.595,
            0.581
          ],
          "content": "For example, adding the digits of the number 68 will be same as adding the digits of 176 or 545."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.593,
            0.353,
            0.615
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.199,
            0.628,
            0.365,
            0.648
          ],
          "content": "**1. Digit sum 14**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.23,
            0.651,
            0.737,
            0.671
          ],
          "content": ".a. Write other numbers whose digits add up to 14."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.813,
            0.628,
            0.899,
            0.681
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_image_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.23,
            0.674,
            0.778,
            0.694
          ],
          "content": "b. What is the smallest number whose digit sum is 14?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.231,
            0.696,
            0.749,
            0.716
          ],
          "content": "c. What is the largest 5-digit whose digit sum is 14?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.232,
            0.719,
            0.805,
            0.762
          ],
          "content": "d. How big a number can you form having the digit sum of 14? Can you make an even bigger number?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.764,
            0.804,
            0.807
          ],
          "content": "2. Find out the digit sums of all the numbers from 40 to 70. Share your observations with the class."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.81,
            0.885,
            0.877
          ],
          "content": "3. Calculate the digit sums of 3-digit numbers whose digits are consecutive (for example, 345). Do you see a pattern? Will this pattern continue?"
        },
        {
